<ResourceDictionary
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!--
        The WPF original styled `l:DockWindow` (WindowStyle=None, BorderThickness=0, Topmost=True,
        ShowInTaskbar=False, AllowsTransparency=True, IsHitTestVisible=True, Background=#01000000,
        SizeToContent=Height) via an implicit `<Style TargetType="l:DockWindow">`.

        WinUI 3's Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Window (and WinUIEx.WindowEx, which derives from it) is not a
        DependencyObject/FrameworkElement, so it cannot be a Style TargetType at all — there is no
        WinUI 3 equivalent of "a ResourceDictionary Style targeting a Window subclass" (see the note
        in SettingsWindow.xaml documenting the same constraint for Window.Resources). Every one of
        the WPF style's settings is applied directly instead, on the WindowEx element in
        DockWindow.xaml or in DockWindow.xaml.cs:
          - WindowStyle=None, BorderThickness=0   -> IsTitleBarVisible="False" (DockWindow.xaml)
          - Topmost=True                          -> IsAlwaysOnTop="True" (DockWindow.xaml)
          - ShowInTaskbar=False                   -> IsShownInSwitchers="False" (DockWindow.xaml;
                                                      WinUI 3 has no separate taskbar-visibility knob)
          - AllowsTransparency / Background        -> superseded by DesktopAcrylicBackdrop
            (#01000000)                               (DockWindow.xaml.cs); WPF's near-transparent
                                                      hit-testing trick doesn't apply in WinUI 3 (see
                                                      DockWindow.xaml's own Background="Transparent")
          - IsHitTestVisible=True                  -> WinUI 3 elements are hit-testable by default;
                                                      no equivalent setter needed
          - SizeToContent=Height                   -> not ported: WindowEx/Window expose no
                                                      SizeToContent equivalent in this WinUIEx
                                                      version. Documented as a known gap in this
                                                      task's report rather than silently dropped.

        This dictionary is intentionally empty: nothing here needs to survive as an actual
        ResourceDictionary entry, but the file (and DockWindow.xaml's merge of it) is kept for
        structural parity with the WPF original per this plan's precedent.
    -->
</ResourceDictionary>
